# Line endings are LF in the repository AND in the working tree, on every
# machine, regardless of anyone's core.autocrlf setting.
#
# Not just tidiness: a CRLF checkout puts carriage returns inside multi-line
# template literals (BlogPostPage.tsx has a `className` string spanning eight
# lines), so those \r characters end up in the built bundle. That changes the
# chunk's content hash, which cascades through every asset filename — and the
# committed dist/ then disagrees with a rebuild for no reason anyone can see.
# Pinning eol=lf makes a build depend on the source alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch scripts are the exception — cmd.exe mis-parses LF-only files.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never normalise, never diff as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.eot  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.zip  binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pptx binary
*.docx binary
